      {
        "type": "GeneralText",
        "content": "<h2>About&nbsp;the&nbsp;Major&nbsp;in&nbsp;Ancient&nbsp;Greek&nbsp;&amp;&nbsp;Roman&nbsp;Studies&nbsp;(AGRS)</h2><p>The&nbsp;major&nbsp;in&nbsp;Ancient&nbsp;Greek&nbsp;and&nbsp;Roman&nbsp;Studies&nbsp;(AGRS)&nbsp;invites&nbsp;you&nbsp;to&nbsp;explore&nbsp;the&nbsp;rich&nbsp;diversity&nbsp;of&nbsp;the&nbsp;ancient&nbsp;Mediterranean&nbsp;world&nbsp;through&nbsp;a&nbsp;dynamic,&nbsp;interdisciplinary&nbsp;lens.&nbsp;</p><p>Housed&nbsp;within&nbsp;the&nbsp;Department&nbsp;of&nbsp;Ancient&nbsp;Greek&nbsp;&amp;&nbsp;Roman&nbsp;Studies&nbsp;(DAGRS),&nbsp;our&nbsp;curriculum&nbsp;features&nbsp;a&nbsp;vibrant&nbsp;selection&nbsp;of&nbsp;literary,&nbsp;historical,&nbsp;philosophical,&nbsp;and&nbsp;archaeological&nbsp;courses&nbsp;taught&nbsp;entirely&nbsp;in&nbsp;English&nbsp;and&nbsp;translation.&nbsp;</p><p>You&nbsp;can&nbsp;deep-dive&nbsp;into&nbsp;ancient&nbsp;myth,&nbsp;explore&nbsp;classical&nbsp;thought,&nbsp;and&nbsp;study&nbsp;material&nbsp;culture&nbsp;without&nbsp;prior&nbsp;knowledge&nbsp;of&nbsp;Greek&nbsp;or&nbsp;Latin.</p><p>While&nbsp;ancient&nbsp;language&nbsp;study&nbsp;remains&nbsp;an&nbsp;available&nbsp;and&nbsp;enriching&nbsp;option&nbsp;for&nbsp;interested&nbsp;students,&nbsp;it&nbsp;is&nbsp;entirely&nbsp;optional&nbsp;for&nbsp;admission&nbsp;and&nbsp;degree&nbsp;completion.</p><p></p><p>Students&nbsp;in&nbsp;AGRS&nbsp;join&nbsp;a&nbsp;small,&nbsp;supportive&nbsp;cohort.&nbsp;The&nbsp;thorough&nbsp;training&nbsp;you&nbsp;receive&nbsp;prepares&nbsp;you&nbsp;for&nbsp;a&nbsp;wide&nbsp;range&nbsp;of&nbsp;professional&nbsp;paths,&nbsp;including&nbsp;law,&nbsp;medicine,&nbsp;teaching,&nbsp;and&nbsp;business.</p><p></p><p>As&nbsp;a&nbsp;specialized&nbsp;academic&nbsp;path,&nbsp;AGRS&nbsp;is&nbsp;intended&nbsp;for&nbsp;students&nbsp;whose&nbsp;primary&nbsp;academic&nbsp;passions&nbsp;align&nbsp;with&nbsp;this&nbsp;curriculum.&nbsp;Because&nbsp;of&nbsp;the&nbsp;program's&nbsp;focused&nbsp;nature,&nbsp;we&nbsp;seek&nbsp;students&nbsp;who&nbsp;are&nbsp;fully&nbsp;committed&nbsp;to&nbsp;completing&nbsp;their&nbsp;undergraduate&nbsp;degree&nbsp;in&nbsp;this&nbsp;specific&nbsp;major&nbsp;and&nbsp;scholarly&nbsp;community.</p><p></p><h2>Direct&nbsp;Admission&nbsp;to&nbsp;the&nbsp;Major</h2><p>When&nbsp;you&nbsp;are&nbsp;admitted&nbsp;to&nbsp;UC&nbsp;Berkeley&nbsp;for&nbsp;Ancient&nbsp;Greek&nbsp;and&nbsp;Roman&nbsp;Studies&nbsp;(AGRS),&nbsp;you&nbsp;enter&nbsp;directly&nbsp;into&nbsp;the&nbsp;major.&nbsp;There&nbsp;is&nbsp;no&nbsp;secondary&nbsp;application&nbsp;or&nbsp;declaration&nbsp;process&nbsp;after&nbsp;you&nbsp;arrive&nbsp;on&nbsp;campus.&nbsp;</p><p>You&nbsp;are&nbsp;a&nbsp;full&nbsp;member&nbsp;of&nbsp;our&nbsp;department&nbsp;from&nbsp;day&nbsp;one.</p><p></p><p>While&nbsp;it&nbsp;is&nbsp;possible&nbsp;to&nbsp;change&nbsp;your&nbsp;major&nbsp;after&nbsp;you&nbsp;matriculate&nbsp;to&nbsp;Berkeley,&nbsp;switching&nbsp;into&nbsp;a&nbsp;high-demand&nbsp;field&nbsp;like&nbsp;Business,&nbsp;Computer&nbsp;Science,&nbsp;Economics,&nbsp;or&nbsp;Psychology&nbsp;may&nbsp;require&nbsp;you&nbsp;to&nbsp;pass&nbsp;a&nbsp;competitive&nbsp;comprehensive&nbsp;review&nbsp;process.&nbsp;Additionally,&nbsp;spending&nbsp;your&nbsp;time&nbsp;preparing&nbsp;for&nbsp;a&nbsp;different&nbsp;program&nbsp;once&nbsp;you&nbsp;arrive&nbsp;on&nbsp;campus&nbsp;will&nbsp;cause&nbsp;a&nbsp;lack&nbsp;of&nbsp;progress&nbsp;in&nbsp;your&nbsp;currently&nbsp;declared&nbsp;major,&nbsp;which&nbsp;can&nbsp;delay&nbsp;your&nbsp;graduation.&nbsp;</p><p>We&nbsp;want&nbsp;to&nbsp;ensure&nbsp;you&nbsp;choose&nbsp;the&nbsp;path&nbsp;that&nbsp;best&nbsp;supports&nbsp;your&nbsp;long-term&nbsp;goals&nbsp;and&nbsp;allows&nbsp;you&nbsp;to&nbsp;graduate&nbsp;on&nbsp;time.</p><p></p><p><strong style=\"font-size: 14px;\">Personal&nbsp;Advising&nbsp;&amp;&nbsp;Your&nbsp;Transition</strong></p><p>To&nbsp;support&nbsp;a&nbsp;smooth&nbsp;transition,&nbsp;all&nbsp;admitted&nbsp;transfer&nbsp;students&nbsp;are&nbsp;required&nbsp;to&nbsp;meet&nbsp;with&nbsp;our&nbsp;undergraduate&nbsp;advisor&nbsp;before&nbsp;enrolling&nbsp;in&nbsp;their&nbsp;first&nbsp;semester&nbsp;of&nbsp;classes.</p><p>This&nbsp;is&nbsp;our&nbsp;way&nbsp;of&nbsp;welcoming&nbsp;you&nbsp;and&nbsp;ensuring&nbsp;your&nbsp;academic&nbsp;plan&nbsp;matches&nbsp;your&nbsp;interests&nbsp;and&nbsp;graduation&nbsp;goals.</p><p></p><p>You&nbsp;will&nbsp;receive&nbsp;detailed&nbsp;instructions&nbsp;on&nbsp;how&nbsp;to&nbsp;schedule&nbsp;this&nbsp;meeting&nbsp;well&nbsp;before&nbsp;your&nbsp;first&nbsp;semester&nbsp;begins,&nbsp;either&nbsp;through&nbsp;the&nbsp;summer&nbsp;Golden&nbsp;Bear&nbsp;Advising&nbsp;program&nbsp;or&nbsp;via&nbsp;a&nbsp;direct&nbsp;email&nbsp;from&nbsp;our&nbsp;department.&nbsp;</p><p>We&nbsp;look&nbsp;forward&nbsp;to&nbsp;meeting&nbsp;you&nbsp;and&nbsp;helping&nbsp;you&nbsp;plan&nbsp;your&nbsp;time&nbsp;at&nbsp;Berkeley.</p><p></p><h2>Preparing&nbsp;for&nbsp;the&nbsp;Ancient&nbsp;Greek&nbsp;and&nbsp;Roman&nbsp;Studies&nbsp;Major</h2><p>Because&nbsp;introductory&nbsp;courses&nbsp;in&nbsp;ancient&nbsp;history&nbsp;and&nbsp;culture&nbsp;can&nbsp;vary&nbsp;widely&nbsp;across&nbsp;colleges,&nbsp;your&nbsp;best&nbsp;initial&nbsp;preparation&nbsp;is&nbsp;to&nbsp;focus&nbsp;on&nbsp;completing&nbsp;your&nbsp;General&nbsp;Education&nbsp;(GE)&nbsp;requirements&nbsp;at&nbsp;your&nbsp;current&nbsp;institution.&nbsp;</p><p>Getting&nbsp;these&nbsp;broad&nbsp;university&nbsp;requirements&nbsp;out&nbsp;of&nbsp;the&nbsp;way&nbsp;clears&nbsp;your&nbsp;schedule,&nbsp;giving&nbsp;you&nbsp;the&nbsp;flexibility&nbsp;to&nbsp;dive&nbsp;into&nbsp;our&nbsp;specialized&nbsp;coursework&nbsp;once&nbsp;you&nbsp;arrive&nbsp;at&nbsp;Berkeley.</p><p></p><p>The&nbsp;major&nbsp;includes&nbsp;three&nbsp;to&nbsp;four&nbsp;lower-division&nbsp;courses&nbsp;(note&nbsp;that&nbsp;community&nbsp;college&nbsp;courses&nbsp;articulate&nbsp;to&nbsp;the&nbsp;university&nbsp;as&nbsp;lower-division).&nbsp;</p><p>While&nbsp;not&nbsp;strictly&nbsp;required&nbsp;for&nbsp;admission,&nbsp;the&nbsp;following&nbsp;subjects&nbsp;are&nbsp;excellent&nbsp;preparation&nbsp;for&nbsp;our&nbsp;curriculum:</p><p></p><ul><li>Classical&nbsp;(Greaco-Roman)&nbsp;Mythology</li><li>Greek&nbsp;Civilization</li><li>Roman&nbsp;Civilization</li><li>Archaeology&nbsp;of&nbsp;the&nbsp;Graeco-Roman&nbsp;World</li><li>Premodern&nbsp;Comparative&nbsp;Culture:&nbsp;One&nbsp;course&nbsp;focusing&nbsp;on&nbsp;the&nbsp;pre-modern&nbsp;world&nbsp;outside&nbsp;of&nbsp;Greece&nbsp;or&nbsp;Rome&nbsp;(e.g.,&nbsp;Ancient&nbsp;Egypt,&nbsp;Pre-Columbian&nbsp;America,&nbsp;China,&nbsp;Japan,&nbsp;or&nbsp;Celtic&nbsp;Civilization).</li></ul><p></p><p><strong>Optional&nbsp;Language&nbsp;Preparation</strong></p><p></p><p>If&nbsp;your&nbsp;college&nbsp;offers&nbsp;them,&nbsp;beginning&nbsp;sequences&nbsp;in&nbsp;Ancient&nbsp;Greek&nbsp;or&nbsp;Latin&nbsp;are&nbsp;wonderful&nbsp;additions&nbsp;to&nbsp;your&nbsp;preparation,&nbsp;though&nbsp;they&nbsp;are&nbsp;not&nbsp;expected&nbsp;or&nbsp;required&nbsp;for&nbsp;admission&nbsp;to&nbsp;the&nbsp;major.</p><p></p><p class=\"ql-indent-1\"><strong>Note:</strong>&nbsp;All&nbsp;courses&nbsp;intended&nbsp;to&nbsp;meet&nbsp;major&nbsp;requirements&nbsp;must&nbsp;be&nbsp;taken&nbsp;for&nbsp;a&nbsp;letter&nbsp;grade.</p>",
        "groupId": "87e36f45-6887-ef11-8474-000d3a37e3b6",
        "position": 3,
        "area": "General"
      },
      {
        "type": "GeneralTitle",
